Install GCC's own headers with cp rather than with tar.

install-headers-tar pipes one tar into another, and there is no tar in this
bootstrap that can create an archive -- mescc-tools-extra ships untar and
nothing else, so `make install` stopped with "tar: command not found".

install-headers-cp is upstream's own alternative, selected here by the same
mechanism the VMS and Cygwin build platforms use. It copies gcc's include and
include-fixed directories directly and needs nothing beyond coreutils.

This cannot be done from the make command line: the top-level Makefile sets
MAKEOVERRIDES= before descending into gcc, so a command-line
INSTALL_HEADERS_DIR does not reach the sub-make that reads it.

--- a/gcc/config.build
+++ b/gcc/config.build
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 build_xm_file=
 build_xm_defines=
 build_exeext=
-build_install_headers_dir=install-headers-tar
+build_install_headers_dir=install-headers-cp
 build_file_translate=

 # System-specific settings.
